          "text": "S3: Proof strategy and lemma decomposition.\n\n- **Forward / necessity:** Assume `hAllow : ALLOW t`. Apply `(contract t).mp` to derive `GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t`.\n- **Reverse / sufficiency:** Assume `hChecks : GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t`. Apply `(contract t).mpr` to derive `ALLOW t`.\n- Combine both implications with `Iff.intro`.\n\n```lean\ntheorem allow_admissible\n    {Transition : Type}\n    (GBP BD OC ALLOW : Transition \u2192 Prop)\n    (contract : \u2200 t, ALLOW t \u2194 (GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t))\n    (t : Transition) :\n    ALLOW t \u2194 (GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t) := by\n  apply Iff.intro\n  \u00b7 intro hAllow\n    exact (contract t).mp hAllow\n  \u00b7 intro hChecks\n    exact (contract t).mpr hChecks\n```\n\nThis proves necessity and sufficiency only under the stipulated abstract evaluator contract; it does not specify a deployed engine or establish implementation validity."
